-- title:
--   Frobenius series commutes with reduction along p^j-power-related maps
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $O$ and $B$ be commutative rings, and let $\psi,\chi : O \to B$ be ring homomorphisms; write $\bar\psi,\bar\chi : O/pO \to B/pB$ for the induced maps on the quotients by the ideals generated by $p$ (`residueMap`). Fix $j \in \mathbb{N}$ and assume that $\bar\psi(x) = \bar\chi(x)^{p^j}$ for every $x \in O/pO$. Let $e$ be a pair $(e_0,e_1)$ of formal power series in two variables over $O/pO$ (an element of `Series (O ⧸ pIdeal p O)`, i.e. a map $\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,(O/pO)$) each of which has vanishing constant coefficient. Over $B/pB$ consider the pair $\mathrm{frobSeries}$ whose $i$-th component is $X_i^{p^j}$. The assertion is the equality of pairs of power series over $B/pB$
--   $$\mathrm{frobSeries} \circ (\bar\chi)_*e \;=\; (\bar\psi)_*e \circ \mathrm{frobSeries},$$
--   where $(\bar\chi)_*e$ and $(\bar\psi)_*e$ denote the coefficientwise images of $e$ and composition of pairs is componentwise substitution (`Series.comp`); component by component this says $\bigl((\bar\chi)_*e_i\bigr)^{p^j} = \bigl((\bar\psi)_*e_i\bigr)(X_0^{p^j},X_1^{p^j})$.
--
--   This is the naturality of the $p^j$-power (Frobenius) substitution with respect to reduction mod $p$ along two homomorphisms related by the $p^j$-power map, the situation produced by a Frobenius lift. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, in the transport of rigidifications of fake elliptic curves (the `isRigTransport` lemmas).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormal_Rigidified_frobSeries_comp_map_eq_map_comp_frobSeries_of_forall_eq_pow.lean

